Text sources. The harness downloads text at run time; no source text is stored
in this repository.
- United Nations Parallel Corpus v1.0, 2015 test and development sets. Source:
  the United Nations. Ziemski, M., Junczys-Dowmunt, M., and Pouliquen, B. (2016),
  The United Nations Parallel Corpus, Language Resources and Evaluation
  (LREC'16), Portoroz, Slovenia, May 2016. The corpus is made available by the
  United Nations without warranty of any kind under its disclaimer and terms of
  use (https://www.un.org/dgacm/en/content/uncorpus).
- Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org), sentences licensed under CC BY 2.0 FR.
  results/v0.1.0/tatoeba_ids.txt lists Tatoeba sentence ids only.

Tokenizers. Tokenizer files are downloaded from their publishers at run time and
are not included in this repository. Each keeps its own licence (see
config/tokenisers.yaml). tiktoken is MIT-licensed (OpenAI).

Prices in config/prices.yaml are facts read from the vendors' public price
pages on the retrieval date given for each row; the pages themselves are not
reproduced.

Runtime dependencies: tiktoken (MIT), tokenizers (Apache-2.0), sentencepiece
(Apache-2.0), huggingface_hub (Apache-2.0), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), PyYAML (MIT).
No third-party code is copied into this repository.

